# The Dockerfile only COPYs compiled binaries out of target/<profile>/, so nothing else is context —
# not the source, and not the rest of target/ (gigabytes of rlibs and .d files).
*
!target/release/kloudlite
!target/release/kloudlite-api
!target/release/kloudlite-worker
!target/release/kloudlite-agent
!target/release/kloudlite-gateway
!target/release/kloudlite-builder-gate
!target/release/kloudlite-slo
!target/release/kloudlite-controller
!target/release/kl-connect
!target/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/kl
!target/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/dev-image/kl
!target/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/kloudlite-intercept-proxy
!target/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/dev-image/kloudlite-intercept-proxy
!target/dev-image/kloudlite
!target/dev-image/kloudlite-api
!target/dev-image/kloudlite-worker
!target/dev-image/kloudlite-agent
!target/dev-image/kloudlite-gateway
!target/dev-image/kloudlite-builder-gate
!target/dev-image/kloudlite-slo
!target/dev-image/kloudlite-controller
!target/dev-image/kl-connect
!deploy/workspace-image/docker-credential-kl
!deploy/workspace-image/kl-build.sh
!deploy/workspace-image/gitignore-global
# Directory whitelists, not named files: a name whitelist here is what broke the workspace-caches
# merge (a new file landed and nobody added its name). deploy/bench/ holds the bench Dockerfile; the
# bench image installs the harness from its lockfile and runs bench/ and pi/ from source, so those
# are admitted and nothing else of harness/ (node_modules, dist, the Electron app) is.
!deploy/bench/
!harness/package.json
!harness/package-lock.json
!harness/bench/
!harness/pi/
harness/bench/test/
!harness/pi/caveman.md
# The six skills the `skill` tool reads: product words, shipped beside the extension.
!harness/skills/
